monster_from:
ZzzCharacter.cpp, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_HUNTER:

    c->Weapon[0].Type = MODEL_ARQUEBUS;
    c->Object.Scale = 0.95f;

No BlendMesh, no HiddenMesh, no Level - so nothing added, nothing hidden, and no glowing eyes, since RenderEye is gated on c->Level == 1. WSclient.cpp's viewport handler overrides one monster's scale after CreateMonster returns, and it is the Giant's, not this one's. 0.95 is the only line in the client about how big a Hunter is: larger than the plain Goblin and the Beetle Monster at 0.8, smaller than the Elite Goblin at 1.2.
